            {
                "entry_id": "706f8116-2856-394f-98f7-6f2f1dd98306",
                "word": "courbette",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ac173505-5de2-4c81-9c19-8c26095af8bc",
                        "entry_id": "706f8116-2856-394f-98f7-6f2f1dd98306",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "courbettes"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9f33b948-6430-4fff-8278-d6cbccae2555",
                        "entry_id": "706f8116-2856-394f-98f7-6f2f1dd98306",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "courbotte"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46e86595-c9c4-38fa-aa0f-2eabca0a5716",
                        "entry_id": "706f8116-2856-394f-98f7-6f2f1dd98306",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mouvement que le cheval fait en se cabrant et bondissant sur ses postérieurs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1853849d-b2ef-4969-82d3-856bad1b876d",
                                "sense_id": "46e86595-c9c4-38fa-aa0f-2eabca0a5716",
                                "text": "La courbette est un saut pour lequel le cheval doit préalablement avancer ses pieds postérieurs le plus près possible de son centre de gravité, en pliant les angles articulaires de l'arrière-main et en affaissant cette partie ; puis il lève les membres antérieurs en pliant les extrémités sous lui, de manière que l'avant-main se trouve enlevée, à peu près à la moitié de la hauteur à laquelle s'enlève le cheval qui se cabre tout droit. Après avoir pris cette position, il fait un petit bond, proportionné à ses moyens et à ses dispositions, afin de gagner du terrain en avant. Les hanches rabattent et accompagnent avec une cadence basse et tride, les membres de devant dans l'instant où ils retombent à terre."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c54052aa-8b04-3b31-baca-e447715c5245",
                        "entry_id": "706f8116-2856-394f-98f7-6f2f1dd98306",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Action de se courber devant quelqu’un, attitude humble et obséquieuse envers quelqu’un, révérence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3995b31d-d88e-404f-b4b4-64dc9dbbdeb4",
                                "sense_id": "c54052aa-8b04-3b31-baca-e447715c5245",
                                "text": "Faire une courbette."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9c26bcd-a652-4b00-9887-e3e8c6c59806",
                                "sense_id": "c54052aa-8b04-3b31-baca-e447715c5245",
                                "text": "Surtout que je suis assez connu du personnel et des habitués, que j'étais la vedette du jour, et que cela m'a valu une réception du tonnerre avec courbettes, sourires et dos voûtés des maîtres d'hôtel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5c4b9b1-6a97-4d4e-9835-ebd41a53dbde",
                                "sense_id": "c54052aa-8b04-3b31-baca-e447715c5245",
                                "text": "Et ils ricanent, ils s’esclaffent, ils l’invectivent, ils font semblant de l’adorer, ils le supplient, ils s’agenouillent devant lui pour rire, ils lui font des courbettes grotesques, des révérences…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf255e6b-9378-4942-bceb-e39685b8b204",
                                "sense_id": "c54052aa-8b04-3b31-baca-e447715c5245",
                                "text": "L’un après l’autre, les visiteurs se lèvent, esquissent une courbette, marmonnent quelque formule, avant de se rasseoir."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ae31cd8-328c-4fe0-b312-2154c662d316",
                                "sense_id": "c54052aa-8b04-3b31-baca-e447715c5245",
                                "text": "Après quoi, ayant à nouveau baisé la main de ces dames, fait mes courbettes, claqué les talons, je courais joyeusement derrière le dépôt de bois où, coiffé d'un tricorne de papier et armé d'un bâton, je défendais l'Alsace-Lorraine, marchais sur Berlin et accomplissais la conquête du monde jusqu'à l'heure du goûter."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efb166a2-d321-3468-9ab0-95f28cd326bc",
                        "entry_id": "706f8116-2856-394f-98f7-6f2f1dd98306",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Balancier de manœuvre des chaînes des soufflets de forge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9cc59c49-7a1d-36c9-bbf8-067024642304",
                        "entry_id": "706f8116-2856-394f-98f7-6f2f1dd98306",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Action du corps de passer d'une courbe concave faciale à une courbe dorsale, ou inversement, nécessaire à la réalisation d'éléments acrobatiques."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Gymnastique"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7767e174-28da-447c-9eb4-63aeb0bd8e1d",
                        "source_entry_id": "706f8116-2856-394f-98f7-6f2f1dd98306",
                        "source_sense_description": "bond du cheval",
                        "target_lang_word": "curvet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "curvet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf87e3d0-85c7-30fc-b5a1-ace2ae22f15f",
                                        "entry_id": "b071623e-eadd-39ae-ad42-5649c6a08229",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a horse or, by extension, another animal: to leap about, to frolic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1a8a5d5-f489-4472-9fb8-02dfea09106a",
                                                "sense_id": "bf87e3d0-85c7-30fc-b5a1-ace2ae22f15f",
                                                "text": "Sometime he trots, as if he told the steps, / With gentle majesty and modest pride; / Anon he rears upright, curvets and leaps, / As who should say, 'Lo! thus my strength is tried; / And this I do to captivate the eye / Of the fair breeder that is standing by.'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ffbd3ce-b65a-4c00-b91f-e5e286f9e8b1",
                                                "sense_id": "bf87e3d0-85c7-30fc-b5a1-ace2ae22f15f",
                                                "text": "The boy turns into a dog and bow-wows—a cock, he flaps his wings and crows—a cow, he fetches a long drawn moo—a horse broke loose, he curvets, prances and kicks fearfully among his nursery blocks—a big bull, he waxes dangerous as he bellows and paws the carpet—a locomotive, he blows his steam whistle and dashes round the nursery with puffs and yells spasmodic, or taming down, sticks a feather in his cap and struts a soldier."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "618ec9e8-50ac-4b47-8d0f-0f6bacba67f6",
                                                "sense_id": "bf87e3d0-85c7-30fc-b5a1-ace2ae22f15f",
                                                "text": "[T]he dog—a magnificent Newfoundland—that had come galloping down the field to meet us, began curveting round us, in gambols full of graceful beauty, and welcoming us with short joyful barks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95579d3d-dd7e-4715-95aa-bb1417ccc11a",
                                                "sense_id": "bf87e3d0-85c7-30fc-b5a1-ace2ae22f15f",
                                                "text": "Gaily the grey horses curvetted to their destination at the church-gate, a laughter in the whole movement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95329bcb-78c9-4707-8cbc-0050de075259",
                                                "sense_id": "bf87e3d0-85c7-30fc-b5a1-ace2ae22f15f",
                                                "text": "Firelily, under him, seemed sexually aroused, she curveted and frolicked so about the line of march, covering five miles to the prisoners’ one."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0634bf8d-c52a-380a-a8d2-e1ee20066d67",
                                        "entry_id": "b071623e-eadd-39ae-ad42-5649c6a08229",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause to leap about, dart or jump."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f31893e-04c0-4a0c-8bee-c900c008649b",
                                                "sense_id": "0634bf8d-c52a-380a-a8d2-e1ee20066d67",
                                                "text": "[…] I could no more travel the same Path, again and again, than I could have Patience to mount a managed Horse, in the Riding-House, and curvet it in the same Spot, for three Hours together."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e9ce5f7-9c31-4d7b-9c05-e2410d05326a",
                                                "sense_id": "0634bf8d-c52a-380a-a8d2-e1ee20066d67",
                                                "text": "[…] the upright leaden spout, curveting its liquid filament into [the well], is merely a representation of what the gardener himself, if called upon, could do better and more abundantly."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58734d33-18c6-324b-a7ec-9e4c81307a80",
                                        "entry_id": "b071623e-eadd-39ae-ad42-5649c6a08229",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fly or swim with darting movements."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a bird"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdc3e739-4070-4288-91ca-181656795f23",
                                                "sense_id": "58734d33-18c6-324b-a7ec-9e4c81307a80",
                                                "text": "[…] flights of small, low-flying brown doves chased one another to and fro, and bee-eaters, emerald-green, curvetted like slow swallows."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50e755a7-055b-43b4-a28d-27092f2b9c29",
                                                "sense_id": "58734d33-18c6-324b-a7ec-9e4c81307a80",
                                                "text": "The west wind was the music, the motion, the force / To which the swans curveted, a will to change, / A will to make iris frettings on the blank."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0276ae71-f837-491c-bec5-dc8ad5e13ce2",
                                                "sense_id": "58734d33-18c6-324b-a7ec-9e4c81307a80",
                                                "text": "Bank swallows are skimming above the stream, snatching insects, curvetting, rocketing up against the dying light."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6de410c-7627-3955-9e05-f6b5532924ff",
                                        "entry_id": "b071623e-eadd-39ae-ad42-5649c6a08229",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(of a person) To prance; to caper, frolic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65107086-c608-4909-8a4d-586fcba50692",
                                                "sense_id": "e6de410c-7627-3955-9e05-f6b5532924ff",
                                                "text": "He curvetted back into the living-room […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b336fc4f-24e3-4ec0-bcb5-8435b8130022",
                                                "sense_id": "e6de410c-7627-3955-9e05-f6b5532924ff",
                                                "text": "It is not possible, many critics allege, that Juana Inés could have lived in the whirlwind of the court for five years […] and have emerged unscathed. I have already said that it would be absurd to discount the possibility of some curvetting and amorous play."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "692b0dde-ab5e-3d68-a8cf-981fa0561f5f",
                                        "entry_id": "b071623e-eadd-39ae-ad42-5649c6a08229",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(of an object) To jump, skip, shake."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "432cb24d-cfa1-43a3-a299-b8cf830b1371",
                                                "sense_id": "692b0dde-ab5e-3d68-a8cf-981fa0561f5f",
                                                "text": "[…] you must know that when the second iron is thrown overboard, it thenceforth becomes a dangling, sharp-edged terror, skittishly curvetting about both boat and whale, entangling the lines, or cutting them, and making a prodigious sensation in all directions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bfbcecd-e336-49c0-a7bf-eec0889d7e10",
                                                "sense_id": "692b0dde-ab5e-3d68-a8cf-981fa0561f5f",
                                                "text": "The earth shook itself like an animal on whose back a predator has lodged. It spasmed, curvetted, tossed and writhed, to throw that malignity from its shoulders."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "curvet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91a5793b-2741-36e6-8234-fe5f2f63a2e5",
                                        "entry_id": "bbe5059e-a249-3331-9ada-b6b771e0579a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A particular leap in which a horse raises both forelegs at once, equally advanced, and, as the forelegs are falling, raises the hind legs, so that all the legs are in the air at once."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d31e43f-37b8-40f2-9a26-c6d0bf58b09d",
                                                "sense_id": "91a5793b-2741-36e6-8234-fe5f2f63a2e5",
                                                "text": "Complexion and constitution are alike revived by a drive in the Park—a white glove rests on the carriage window—and some 'gallant gray' or chestnut Arabian is curbed into curvets and foam by its whispering master."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f546cc2d-6bc6-3cab-a35d-d13d4105713e",
                                        "entry_id": "bbe5059e-a249-3331-9ada-b6b771e0579a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prank; a frolic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
